    <TTEXTS:has_summary rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">In A Separate Peace, Gene Forrester reflects on his complex friendship with the charismatic Finny at a boys boarding school during World War II, where envy, guilt, and a tragic accident reveal the inner battles of adolescence and the loss of innocence.</TTEXTS:has_summary>
