    <TTEXTS:has_summary rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">In And the Mountains Echoed by Khaled Hosseini, a multi-generational, multi-perspective narrative unfolds across continents and decades, centering on the painful separation of siblings Abdullah and Pari in 1950s Afghanistan, and exploring how this act of sacrifice, memory, and longing reverberates through the lives of those connected to them in profound, often heartbreaking ways.</TTEXTS:has_summary>
    <TTEXTS:has_year_of_publication rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#gYear">2013</TTEXTS:has_year_of_publication>
