    <TTEXTS:has_summary rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Art Spiegelman interviews his father, Vladek, a Polish Jew and Holocaust survivor, to understand his harrowing experiences during World War II. As their strained father-son relationship unfolds alongside the graphic depiction of survival, Maus explores memory, trauma, and the lasting impact of history.</TTEXTS:has_summary>
