    <TTEXTS:has_summary rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">In the span of a single day, Natasha, a science-minded Jamaican immigrant facing deportation, and Daniel, a poetic Korean American torn between duty and desire, meet by chance and form a deep connection. Through alternating perspectives and brief glimpses into the lives of others they encounter, the novel explores themes of love, identity, family, and the cultural and political forces that shape their world.</TTEXTS:has_summary>
